Package: mfcj5720dw-cups
Architecture: amd64 i386
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 cups,
 cups-client,
 cups-filters,
 ghostscript,
Suggests: mfcj5720dw-cups-monitor
Description: native CUPS driver for the Brother MFC-J5720DW
 Independent CUPS Raster filter with a generated PPD, color calibration
 profiles, ink-level reporting, head cleaning and an internal nozzle check.
 The encoder is linked directly into the filter; no Brother LPR executable
 or wrapper is needed. The amd64 build needs no 32-bit compatibility libraries.
 .
 Select Brother MFC-J5720DW CUPS when adding the printer. Removing this package
 deletes local CUPS queues using its filters. Upgrades preserve those queues.

Package: mfcj5720dw-cups-monitor
Section: utils
Architecture: amd64 i386
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 mfcj5720dw-cups (= ${binary:Version}),
 sane-utils,
 tesseract-ocr,
 tesseract-ocr-eng,
 tesseract-ocr-fra,
 xdg-utils,
Suggests:
 brscan4,
 gnome-shell-extension-appindicator,
Description: desktop status monitor for the Brother MFC-J5720DW
 GTK application displaying printer status, detailed faults and ink levels,
 with a tray icon, notifications, English/French interfaces and optional
 login startup. A maintenance window offers head cleaning and nozzle checks.
 .
 Optional scan-to-PC support receives requests from the printer's front panel
 and saves PDF, JPEG or searchable PDF files, or opens an email draft with a
 PDF attachment. Scanning requires Brother's separately installed 64-bit
 brscan4 SANE backend; printing and status monitoring work without it.
